# Proofs for the conditions palletStation.rcs generates, measured against Isabelle2025-2
# on 2026-09-22. 36 of 62 close; what the other 26 need is recorded at the bottom.
#
#   java -jar target/ReflexVCG-1.0-jar-with-dependencies.jar \
#        -s src/test/resources/programs-new/palletStation.rcs -o target/isa-check
#   tools/check-with-isabelle.sh target/isa-check PalletStationTheory \
#        --proofs tools/palletStation.proofs
#
# A condition's name carries the number it was written under, and those shift whenever the
# program does. Regenerate this file rather than renumbering it by hand.

@simp = using assms by (simp add: setVarVal_def constants_def inv_def)
@auto = using assms by (auto simp add: setVarVal_def constants_def inv_def substate_refl loopInv0_def loopInv1_def loopInv2_def loopInv3_def loopInv4_def)

# --- loops -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Every entry, every variant bound, every variant decrease, and six of the seven steps.
# The bounds and decreases need no case analysis, so simp is enough; the entries and steps
# have to instantiate the invariant at a state, which needs auto and substate_refl.
LOOPENTRY14	@auto
LOOPENTRY26	@auto
LOOPENTRY34	@auto
LOOPENTRY45	@auto
LOOPENTRY50	@auto
LOOPSTEP16	@auto
LOOPSTEP28	@auto
LOOPSTEP30	@auto
LOOPSTEP36	@auto
LOOPSTEP38	@auto
LOOPSTEP52	@auto
LOOPBOUND15	@simp
LOOPBOUND27	@simp
LOOPBOUND35	@simp
LOOPBOUND46	@simp
LOOPBOUND51	@simp
LOOPDECREASE17	@simp
LOOPDECREASE29	@simp
LOOPDECREASE31	@simp
LOOPDECREASE37	@simp
LOOPDECREASE39	@simp
LOOPDECREASE48	@simp
LOOPDECREASE53	@simp

# --- annotations -----------------------------------------------------------------------
ASSERT2	@simp
ASSERT5	@simp
ASSERT7	@simp
ASSERT10	@simp
ASSERT18	@auto
ASSERT54	@auto
ASSERT56	@auto
ASSERT60	@auto
ASSUME33	@simp
ASSUME44	@simp
ASSUME49	@auto

# --- cycles ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
VC59	@auto
VC61	@auto

# =========================================================================================
# Open, and why. None of these is a malformed lemma; each is a claim that does not follow.
#
# LOOPSTEP47 - a generator defect, and the only one here. The inner loop's exit state is
#   opaque and declared toEnvP, which makes it a boundary of the *outer* loop's run too, so
#   the outer invariant is demanded half-way through an outer iteration, where
#   placed = r*COLS + COLS and the invariant says placed = r*COLS. Restricted to the
#   iteration's end the step proves with @auto; restricted to the inner loop's exit state it
#   is not provable. This is what forces the per-loop toLoop/toLoopP pair the specification
#   asks for and ReflexBase.thy lacks - see CLAUDE.md, "Not done yet".
#
# VC0 VC1 VC8 VC9 VC11 VC12 VC20 VC21 VC23 VC24 VC42 VC43 VC58 - the cycle conditions. Each
#   must show all of inv, which conjoins invariants palletStation does not implement:
#   nothing stops the belts on jam, and nothing bounds the time spent in packing. One false
#   conjunct sinks the whole condition. The machinery underneath is sound - VC8 restricted
#   to the conjuncts the program does establish proves with @auto, induction across the
#   cycle boundary included.
#
# ASSERT3 ASSERT6 ASSERT19 ASSERT22 ASSERT32 ASSERT40 ASSERT41 ASSERT55 ASSERT57
# ASSUME4 ASSUME13 ASSUME25 - annotations that state more than their path establishes: an
#   assume over a free input the environment supplies, a claim about an earlier cycle that
#   inv does not record, or (ASSERT6) next(...), which asks about a boundary the path has
#   not reached. palletStation is written to exercise every operator, not to satisfy what it
#   claims, so several of its annotations are simply false of it.
